
row          vg8020        cf3300            zb   what it asks
f.g0            7 0           7 0           0 0   GOSUB depth 1 -- the floor
f.g10          70 0          70 0       22865 7   GOSUB depth 10
f.g20         140 0         140 0       22865 7   GOSUB depth 20 -- must be ~2x f.g10 if linear
f.n10         320 0         320 0       22840 7   10 nested GOSUB+FOR pairs

reads `[FRE(0)@top - FRE(0)@depth N   ERR]`  (ERR 0 = it got there)
  ~7*N  -> the control frames come out of the SAME memory FRE(0) reports
  0     -> they are somewhere else entirely

bytes per GOSUB level, from FRE(0):
  vg8020   depth 1/10/20 cost      7     70    140 B   marginal 7.0 then 7.0 B/level
  cf3300   depth 1/10/20 cost      7     70    140 B   marginal 7.0 then 7.0 B/level
  zb       COULD NOT REACH: f.g10 (ERR 7), f.g20 (ERR 7)  <- the depth cap IS the outcome, not a missing reading
